## Why two licenses

Open-source software licenses and "non-commercial" terms don't mix well:
programmers reusing a script shouldn't inherit a ban on commercial use.
So the ideas and writing stay protected (credit, non-commercial,
share-alike), while the tools stay genuinely open.
